+2.  **Robust Z-Score Normalization:**
+    The measures $C_i^{mean}$, $C_i^{max}$, and $G_i^{mean}$ have different numerical ranges. Apply robust z-score normalization to reduce sensitivity to extreme values [S1]:
     $$ z(x) = \frac{x - \text{median}(x)}{\text{median}(|x - \text{median}(x)|) + \epsilon} $$
-    where $\text{median}(x)$ is the median of measure $x$ over all Gaussians [S1].
