+
+4.  **Select Pairs:**
+    *   Select the top $M_{eff}^{LC}$ Gaussians with the highest $s_i^{LC}$ scores as LC candidates.
+    *   Select the top $M_{eff}^{HE}$ Gaussians with the highest $s_i^{HE}$ scores as HE candidates.
+    *   The number of relocated pairs $M$ is determined by the smaller effective sample size:
+        $$ M_{eff}^q = \frac{1}{\sum_{j=1}^N (p_j^q)^2} $$
+        $$ M = \min(M_{eff}^{LC}, M_{eff}^{HE}) $$
